WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.380
In this video, you generate a template from an existing virtual machine and use it to create a new one, so every copy starts with the same configuration.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:15.400
On the Virtual Machines page, open the action menu of the source virtual machine.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.370
Select Generate Template.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:25.850
Leave With Data cleared. The template then points to the original image instead of copying the disk contents.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.880
Name the template.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.670
Select Create.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:37.560
The template appears under Advanced, Templates. It has one version, which is also its default.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:43.950
To use it, create a new virtual machine in the same namespace as the template.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.850
Give it a name.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.590
Select Use the virtual machine template.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.910
Choose the template. Its default version is selected for you.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:01:02.070
The CPU, memory, disks, and network now come from the template. You can still change them here.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.060
Select Create.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:12.990
The new virtual machine is running, with the same configuration as its source.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:19.354
You can now create identical virtual machines from the template. Next, you clone an existing virtual machine.
